course: dictionary
lesson: 2170
title: Correction, putting things right
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A correction is a change that makes something right that was wrong. When your teacher marks a mistake and you fix it, you are doing a correction. «Do your corrections before you hand in the test» means fix the mistakes your teacher marked.
explain: Correction can also be the act of putting mistakes right. Correction fluid and correction tape cover a mistake so you can write the right answer. In maths, checking and correcting your answers is good practice, so look for the clues: a teacher's mark, a rubbed-out word or a changed number.
explain: The word has more than one meaning, so use the words around it to choose the right one. «"A correction", on the stock market, means a sharp fall in prices» is about money, not school. The stock market is where shares, small parts of companies, are bought and sold. Ask yourself: does this sentence talk about school, money or bikes?
explain: In formal, old-fashioned writing, correction can mean punishment, as in old prisons. You will not often see this meaning, but a dictionary will tell you when you need it.
fact: A correction is a change that makes something right that was wrong.
fact: «Corrections» is the plural of correction: it means more than one change.
fact: Correction can mean the act of putting mistakes right, like using correction tape to cover an error.
fact: On the stock market, a correction is a sharp fall in prices.
fact: In formal, old-fashioned use, correction can mean punishment, as in old prisons.
exercise: «Do your corrections before you hand in the test.» What are corrections here? | *Changes that put right the mistakes that were wrong | Questions that have no answer | Mistakes that you make on purpose | Pages from a library book
exercise: Maths tip: checking and correction of answers is good practice. In this sentence, what does correction mean? | *Putting right the answers that were wrong | Shouting out the answer | Adding up a long column of numbers | Writing in pencil instead of pen
exercise: Find and copy the plural of correction from this sentence: «Corrections are usually much smaller than the false stories they correct.» | false | stories | they | *Corrections
test: On the stock market, what does «a correction» mean? | Putting mistakes right in a school book | A small turn of a bicycle wheel | A kind of punishment in an old prison | *A sharp fall in prices
test: A bike rider makes small corrections to the front wheel to stay balanced. What are these corrections? | Punishments for bad riding | Big jumps off the path | Sharp falls in prices | *Tiny steering changes that bring the wheels back under the rider
exam: «A good news source owns its mistakes by printing corrections.» Why is this a sign you can trust it more? | *It admits its mistakes openly, which shows it can be trusted | Corrections are always very big and frightening | It hides its mistakes from the readers | It never makes any mistakes at all
